# AlphaLens — Integrations

Every external service is behind an internal interface. Controllers never call third-party APIs directly.

Registry: `docs/integrations.md`. Market-data vendor decision: `docs/market-data-provider-decision.md`. Do not implement a production market-data adapter until `docs/data-licensing.md` names a signed commercial display/storage contract.

## Required provider interfaces

```text
MarketDataProvider → ProviderA, ProviderB (start with mock)
NewsProvider
AIProvider
BrokerProvider
NotificationProvider
```

Example:

```java
public interface MarketDataProvider {
    StockQuote getQuote(String instrumentId);
    List<Candle> getHistoricalData(
        String instrumentId, Timeframe timeframe, LocalDate from, LocalDate to);
}

public interface BrokerProvider {
    AccountInfo getAccount();
    List<Holding> getHoldings();
    List<Position> getPositions();
    OrderResult placeOrder(OrderRequest request);
    OrderResult modifyOrder(OrderRequest request);
    OrderResult cancelOrder(String orderId);
}
```

Initial broker implementation: `KiteBrokerProvider`. Future: Upstox, Dhan, Angel, FYERS. Zerodha-specific types must not leak into the core domain.

## Market data licensing

Never assume a broker API can legally be used as the commercial market-data source.

Before production redistribution: identify the provider; verify licensing, redistribution, and commercial use; document in `docs/data-licensing.md`.

If licensing is unclear: **stop** production market-data implementation and use a mock provider.

Never hard-code market data. Chart data comes from our backend. The frontend must not call the external market-data provider.

## Charting (when Phase 7 is authorized)

TradingView Lightweight Charts. Support candlestick, line, area, volume, crosshair, zoom, pan, multiple timeframes.

Initial timeframes: `1D 1W 1M 6M 1Y 5Y MAX`.

Initial indicators (Phase 8 only): SMA, EMA, RSI, MACD, VWAP, Bollinger Bands. Do not implement 30+ indicators initially.

## AI (Phase 20 only)

`AIProvider` receives structured calculated data and explains it. AI must not calculate PE, CAGR, ROCE, DCF, returns, or portfolio allocation.

OpenAI is called from the backend only. Never put API keys in Vue.

## Secrets

Never put Kite `api_secret` or `access_token` in frontend code. Keep broker tokens server-side and encrypted. Never expose database credentials to the frontend.

## Notifications

Use a notification abstraction. Do not hard-code email-provider logic into business services.

## Trading safety (Phase 24 only)

Always show a confirmation screen. Never place an order solely because an algorithm generated a signal. Require explicit user confirmation unless a separately reviewed automated-trading feature is intentionally introduced.
